          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Decorated cospans are a convenient formalism to deal with open networks, i.e. networks where some nodes are interpreted to be ‘inputs’ and some other to be ‘outputs’. In fact, a natural way to do such labelling is to specify some function assigning the set of inputs to those nodes in the network tasked with receiving them, and analogously, a function assigning to outputs those nodes which provide them. This is, morally, a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cospan"} cospan
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FinSet"} FinSet
            = succeed "." do
              %em decoration
          %p Surprisingly, this formalism naturally captures also other operations such as sequential and parallel composition of networks.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#categories_of_cospans Categories of cospans
          %p
            In a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf C
            with finite colimits (or even just
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushouts
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cospans"} cospans
            can be composed in a natural way. In fact, given
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo →
                  %mi s
                  %mo ←
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \to s \leftarrow y
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo →
                    %mi t
                    %mo ←
                    %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \to t \leftarrow z
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo →
                  %mi p
                  %mo ←
                  %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \to p \leftarrow z
            by taking a pushout in the middle:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi s
                          %msub
                            %mo +
                            %mi y
                          %mi t
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi p
                                %mi s
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo ↖
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi p
                                %mi t
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi s
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi t
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mi f
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo ↖
                            %mi g
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mi h
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo ↖
                            %mi i
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi x
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi y
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp; s +_y t
                  \\\&amp;
                  \&amp;&amp;
                  {}^{p_s}\nearrow
                  \&amp;&amp; \nwarrow^{p_t}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; s &amp;&amp;&amp;&amp; t
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}^{f}\nearrow
                  \&amp;&amp; \nwarrow^{g}
                  \&amp;
                  \&amp; {}^{h}\nearrow
                  \&amp;&amp; \nwarrow^{i}
                  \\\
                  x
                  \&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;
                  y
                  \&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;
                  z
                  }
          %p
            Therefore cospans form a compositional structure: a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Cospan
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Cospan}(\mathbf C)
            where objects are the same of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf C
            but morphisms from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            are replaced by cospans with feet
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            = succeed "-category." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo →
                  %mi p
                  %mo ←
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo →
                  %mi q
                  %mo ←
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x \to p \leftarrow y) \Rightarrow (x \to q \leftarrow y)
            are given by any
            = succeed "-morphism" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi η
                  %mo :
                  %mi p
                  %mo →
                  %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta : p \to q
            making the following commute
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi p
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mi f
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo ↖
                            %mi g
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi x
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi η
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi z
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mrow
                            %mrow
                              %mi f
                              %mo ′
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ↙
                            %mrow
                              %mi g
                              %mo ′
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; p
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}^{f}\nearrow &amp;&amp; \nwarrow^{g}
                  \\\
                  x &amp;&amp;\downarrow^\eta&amp;&amp; z
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}_{f'}\searrow
                  \&amp;&amp; \swarrow_{g'}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; q
                  }
          %p
            It is also customary to ignore the
